# Body-connected electronics and CAD

- Always preserve a battery-powered and independently isolated body-connected boundary; no direct connection of mains-powered bench instruments while electrodes are worn.
- Until qualified electrical safety review, custom EEG acquisition boards are bench-test-only with simulators/dummy loads. Not for human contact.
- Record PCB revisions, part traceability, electrical safety hazards, test rigs, mechanical electrode pressure, contact materials and emergency disconnect behavior.
- Keep CAD manufacturing files and schematics versioned; binary designs need reproducible exports and source/license provenance.
- A hardware change that could affect leakage, isolation, input protection, current paths, power management or electrode contact requires owner approval and an explicit safety ADR.
